{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.38, "text": "Hello and welcome to Videojug. We're going to show you how to make chicken ramen."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 5.1, "end": 9.2, "text": "Step 1. You'll need the following ingredients to serve 2."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 10.64, "end": 12.86, "text": "750 ml of chicken stock."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 13.84, "end": 15.8, "text": "2 tablespoons of peanut oil."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 16.8, "end": 18.92, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 19.9, "end": 21.64, "text": "1 carrot, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 22.54, "end": 25.46, "text": "2 cm of ginger, peeled and chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 26.16, "end": 28.46, "text": "2 garlic cloves, crushed."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 28.46, "end": 31.5, "text": "2 tablespoons of soy sauce."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 32.82, "end": 34.6, "text": "160 grams of noodles."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 36.08, "end": 37.4, "text": "1 large chicken breast."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 38.34, "end": 39.94, "text": "6 oyster mushrooms."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 41.06, "end": 43.0, "text": "2 eggs, hard boiled."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 44.1, "end": 46.18, "text": "1 spring onion, sliced."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 47.2, "end": 48.52, "text": "And salt and pepper."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 50.06, "end": 51.7, "text": "Here is a handy list of the ingredients."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 56.61, "end": 58.47, "text": "You will also need these utensils."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 59.47, "end": 60.69, "text": "2 saucepans."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 60.69, "end": 62.25, "text": "1 wooden spoon."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 62.27, "end": 63.27, "text": "A sieve."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 63.27, "end": 64.27, "text": "A slotted spoon."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 64.27, "end": 65.27, "text": "A chopping board."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 65.27, "end": 66.27, "text": "A knife."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 66.27, "end": 67.27, "text": "A ladle."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 67.27, "end": 68.27, "text": "And a tray."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 68.27, "end": 69.27, "text": "Step 2. Make the broth."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 69.27, "end": 70.27, "text": "Heat one of the saucepans over a moderate temperature and add the peanut oil, followed"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 70.27, "end": 71.27, "text": "by the leeks."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 71.27, "end": 72.27, "text": "Sweat them slightly, then add the carrots, crushed garlic and the ginger and cook for"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 72.27, "end": 73.27, "text": "another 2 to 3 minutes."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 73.27, "end": 74.27, "text": "Add the chicken stock."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 74.27, "end": 75.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 75.27, "end": 76.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 76.27, "end": 77.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 77.27, "end": 78.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 78.27, "end": 79.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 79.27, "end": 80.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 80.27, "end": 81.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 81.27, "end": 82.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 82.27, "end": 83.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 83.27, "end": 84.27, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 84.27, "end": 86.71, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 86.71, "end": 87.53, "text": "1 1⁄2 leeks, chopped."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 87.53, "end": 90.07, "text": "4ikkul paratha, finished."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 90.07, "end": 91.07, "text": "Beat the scones, but don't make all of it."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 91.07, "end": 116.54, "text": "Add 2 stakeholder shouldn, add 1 one"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 116.54, "end": 117.84, "text": "one character, and an expression."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 117.84, "end": 117.88, "text": "Steam for 3 minutes."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 117.88, "end": 118.06, "text": "1 15 minutes."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 118.06, "end": 118.1, "text": "2 10 minutes."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 118.1, "end": 121.98, "text": "and strain the broth. Then put it back on the heat."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 121.98, "end": 125.12, "text": "Step 4. Poach the chicken"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 125.12, "end": 129.58, "text": "and mushrooms. Place the chicken, followed by the mushrooms"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 129.58, "end": 133.28, "text": "into the hot broth. Slowly poach for about seven minutes."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 133.28, "end": 136.56, "text": "Don't let it boil. Keep it over low heat."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 136.56, "end": 139.9, "text": "If the chicken becomes too hot it will dry out."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 139.9, "end": 145.1, "text": "This way it will stay moist. Using the slotted spoon"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 145.1, "end": 148.14, "text": "remove the chicken breast and the mushrooms from the broth"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 148.14, "end": 154.44, "text": "and put aside. Step 5. Cook the noodles."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 154.44, "end": 158.42, "text": "Add the noodles to the broth and raise the heat to a simmer."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 158.42, "end": 163.62, "text": "Leave them to cook for about three minutes. Step 6."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 163.62, "end": 168.98, "text": "Prepare the chicken. Moving lengthwise along the chicken breast"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 168.98, "end": 173.78, "text": "cut into fairly thin slices. Then take the hard-boiled eggs"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 173.78, "end": 178.16, "text": "and chop them in half. Step 7."}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 178.16, "end": 182.36, "text": "Serve. Place the noodles into a soup bowl"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 182.36, "end": 187.36, "text": "and ladle the broth on top. Then arrange the mushrooms on one side"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 187.36, "end": 190.84, "text": "followed by the eggs and chicken"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 190.84, "end": 195.92, "text": "and finally the spring onions. Add a little more broth"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 195.92, "end": 199.64, "text": "and your soup is ready. And that's how to make chicken ramen"}
{"video_id": "2rJ3KKx0oRk", "start": 199.64, "end": 201.12, "text": "the videojug way."}
